 "caption": "Segmentation and own uncertainty of every method on Replica room\\_0 (frame 18), Replica room\\_1 (frame 66), Replica office\\_1 (frame 25), Replica office\\_2 (frame 75), Replica office\\_3 (frame 15), Replica office\\_4 (frame 29), ScanNet scene0070\\_00 (frame 46), ScanNet scene0097\\_00 (frame 2), ScanNet scene0140\\_00 (frame 57), ScanNet scene0200\\_00 (frame 36), ScanNet scene0347\\_00 (frame 0), ScanNet scene0400\\_00 (frame 0), ScanNet scene0590\\_00 (frame 104) and ScanNet scene0645\\_00 (frame 156). Every test scene, at the evaluation frame with the most ground-truth classes that cover at least 0.5\\% of its labeled pixels (a rule on the labels only, fixed before rendering). Row 1: the 3DGS render and the labels (black: no decision); row 2: the ground truth and the errors (vermillion: wrong; black: not scored); row 3: each method's own uncertainty, NormLift's $1-C_{\\mathrm{inter}}$, the learned $u$ of LEGaussians and our $u^{\\mathrm{ale}}$, as its rank among the covered labeled pixels with a defined value in all evaluation frames of the scene (grey: undefined; black: not covered). The 2D features and Feature 3DGS have no own uncertainty (-- in Table~\\ref{tab:replica}); we show no P2 confidence. Numbers are per-scene values over all evaluation frames, read from Table~\\ref{tab:replica}: mIoU (row 1) and the AUSE of the own uncertainty (row 3), in \\%. LEGaussians $\\lambda_u$ = 4 (Replica), 1 (ScanNet), chosen on validation.",
